#X obj 667 11 symbol2any;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 267 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object takes a symbol or a string and interprets
its text as a Pd message. Words separated by spaces become the atoms
of the resulting message \, numbers are converted to floats \, and
the first word is treated as the message selector. This is useful for
building messages dynamically from strings produced by external sources
or by string processing objects.;
#X text 240 199 Use case in algorithmic composition: generating control
messages from text. A composer can store score instructions in a text
file as lines such as "freq 440" or "amp 0.7" and read them one by
one with [textfile]. Passing each line through [symbol2any] turns it
into a real Pd message that can be routed to the corresponding parameter
of a synthesis patch \, which makes the score easy to edit outside
of Pd.;
